WEBVTT

00:02.440 --> 00:04.150
I-I'm so sorry!

00:04.910 --> 00:07.570
Oh, look who we have here.

00:09.920 --> 00:12.360
It's been a while, Maki.

00:13.590 --> 00:15.100
Dad?

00:15.100 --> 00:17.000
What are you doing here?

00:18.300 --> 00:21.220
What am I saying? 
You're here to hang out, I imagine.

00:21.220 --> 00:23.520
You're a high schooler now, after all.

00:23.520 --> 00:26.920
Actually, nah. I came shopping.

00:26.920 --> 00:31.600
I last saw you before summer break, right?

00:32.140 --> 00:32.900
Yeah.

00:33.790 --> 00:39.020
I'm sorry. I should've made time 
to see you again,

00:39.020 --> 00:42.270
but I got busy with work after that.

00:43.430 --> 00:45.190
Are you here for work, then?

00:45.190 --> 00:48.940
Yeah. I happen to have a new client here.

00:49.230 --> 00:51.020
I'm on my way back from a meeting.

00:51.020 --> 00:53.820
Sounds hectic. 
Are you taking care of yourself?

00:53.820 --> 00:55.450
Don't worry about me.

00:57.020 --> 00:59.040
I'm built for this.

01:01.200 --> 01:02.210
Chief Maehara.

01:03.870 --> 01:05.460
I apologize for interrupting.

01:06.440 --> 01:08.700
You were gone for some time, 
so I came to check on you.

01:08.700 --> 01:11.470
Yeah, sorry to keep you waiting.

01:11.470 --> 01:14.470
Minato, this is my son Maki.

01:15.150 --> 01:16.850
Your son...

01:19.210 --> 01:22.140
It's nice to meet you. 
My name is Minato Kyouka.

01:22.140 --> 01:26.100
Er, I'm Maehara Maki. Hello.

01:26.980 --> 01:30.990
TODAY

SORRY TO BARGE IN ON YOUR DATE

SERIOUSLY, IT'S NOT LIKE THAT...
ANYWAY, TOMORROW AFTER SCHOOL.

NOT DONE YET, MAKI?

MAKI-KUN! MEAT'S WAITING!

01:28.260 --> 01:30.150
Friends you're here with?

01:30.150 --> 01:30.990
Yeah.

01:31.410 --> 01:35.270
Well, you seem busy, so I'll head out now.

01:35.270 --> 01:36.860
Yeah, see you.

01:41.460 --> 01:43.330
DIVORCE NOTICE

01:42.280 --> 01:44.460
Why are you always like this?

01:44.940 --> 01:46.920
Why do you never say anything?!

01:47.710 --> 01:48.960
Dad...

01:49.740 --> 01:52.540
Forgive me, Maki.

01:59.020 --> 02:02.430
Took you long enough, Maki. 
Did you get lost?

02:03.020 --> 02:04.850
Something like that.

02:04.850 --> 02:09.570
Umi was all fidgety until 
we saw you coming back.

02:10.230 --> 02:13.740
Enough small talk. Let's get going.

02:14.030 --> 02:16.380
Come on, Maki.

03:47.000 --> 03:50.710
YAKINIKU QUEEN
2 HOUR ALL-YOU-CAN-EAT BBQ

03:47.950 --> 03:50.710
Maki... Are you listening?

03:50.980 --> 03:52.060
Maki!

03:52.510 --> 03:52.980
Hi-yah!

03:52.980 --> 03:53.550
Ow!

03:54.090 --> 03:57.820
Come on. I've been asking you 
what you want to order,

03:57.820 --> 04:01.350
and all you say is "umm" and "ahh."

04:01.710 --> 04:06.720
Space out all you want when you're alone, 
but it's rude to do it in a group.

04:07.390 --> 04:08.360
Sorry.

04:09.800 --> 04:11.930
I guess I'm a little worn out.

04:11.930 --> 04:13.700
Are you okay?

04:13.700 --> 04:17.020
If you're not feeling well, you don't 
have to force yourself to eat.

04:17.020 --> 04:18.440
Nah, I'm good.

04:18.820 --> 04:22.790
I was just spacing out. 
It's not like I'm not hungry.

04:24.460 --> 04:27.960
I'll get the thick beef-tongue cuts.

04:27.960 --> 04:29.920
Hey, that sounds good.

04:30.270 --> 04:34.370
I'm thinking premium skirt. And Yuu?

04:34.370 --> 04:37.510
I'm going with short ribs, obviously.

04:37.510 --> 04:42.880
And let's get some random sausages 
and seafoods to go with it.

04:43.640 --> 04:47.640
Hey! You already went and got ice cream?

04:47.980 --> 04:51.130
And I know it's all-you-can-eat, 
but that's a lot.

04:51.130 --> 04:55.940
You're one to talk. I see your 
childish cola and white soda mix.

04:57.270 --> 05:00.210
Anyway, ice cream doesn't count. 
It goes into a different stomach.

05:01.080 --> 05:03.950
Don't you agree, Maki-kun?

05:03.950 --> 05:06.830
Uh, neither of you can throw stones here.

05:07.180 --> 05:09.740
Umi, you hear that?

05:09.740 --> 05:12.700
You're the childish one here, Yuu!

05:12.700 --> 05:16.710
All I did was experiment with one glass!

05:18.850 --> 05:23.490
In any case, both of you 
need to eat some veggies.

05:31.600 --> 05:33.200
That's mean!

05:31.900 --> 05:34.190
Umi's here. Amami-san's here.

05:34.750 --> 05:35.900
And that's not all.

05:37.040 --> 05:40.150
I know I'll make some 
good memories this year.

05:40.150 --> 05:43.360
So I should forget about last year

05:40.150 --> 05:41.500
No! That'll fill me up!

05:41.500 --> 05:43.360
Just try it!

05:44.330 --> 05:46.510
and think about what's to come.

05:49.980 --> 05:52.040
This should do it.

05:54.630 --> 05:55.360
Heya.

05:55.670 --> 05:56.880
Hey...

05:59.820 --> 06:04.050
It's cold out, so I'd appreciate it
 if you'd let me in.

06:10.070 --> 06:11.640
Here you are.

06:13.160 --> 06:14.350
Thanks.

06:22.340 --> 06:24.720
Did you just sneak a peek at my legs?

06:25.270 --> 06:27.870
It's just, it's winter out, you know?

06:28.200 --> 06:30.350
Yeah, it's real cold.

06:30.350 --> 06:34.920
Frankly, I started to regret it 
on the way here.

06:35.520 --> 06:38.300
You didn't have to wear a skirt, then.

06:38.930 --> 06:40.920
You got me there.

06:41.220 --> 06:45.770
But I want my date to think I'm pretty.

06:45.770 --> 06:46.680
I mean...

06:47.950 --> 06:50.720
You're the boy 
I'm closest with, after all.

06:53.140 --> 06:56.760
So you came here instead of 
meeting up outside because...

06:56.760 --> 07:02.040
Yep. I knew it'd be a bother, 
but I still wanted you to see me ASAP.

07:04.070 --> 07:07.780
Tell me, Maki. How do I look today?

07:08.230 --> 07:09.740
Well...

07:14.750 --> 07:15.720
Never mind!

07:15.720 --> 07:16.540
You know...

07:17.070 --> 07:19.760
It's embarrassing 
saying this to your face...

07:20.400 --> 07:22.650
B-But you're beautiful, Umi.

07:23.580 --> 07:25.540
You took my breath away.

07:26.200 --> 07:28.970
Yeah? Thanks.

07:30.590 --> 07:33.570
I'm glad I put in the effort, then.

07:40.330 --> 07:43.610
Hey, since we're on a date and all,

07:44.380 --> 07:45.820
let's hold hands this way.

07:46.690 --> 07:49.330
Sure. It is quite cold out.

07:49.330 --> 07:52.740
And yet, your hand's awfully sweaty.

07:52.740 --> 07:54.130
Never mind, then.

07:55.870 --> 07:57.090
Not so fast, bucko.

08:01.400 --> 08:05.630
We look like your typical high school 
couple that's trying a bit too hard.

08:06.530 --> 08:11.440
And it's all because Umi dressed me up.

08:12.200 --> 08:17.020
I'm stuck with my looks, and I don't 
really care what anyone says about that.

08:18.300 --> 08:24.280
But I don't want anyone making fun of the 
girl who still says she loves me over it.

08:27.310 --> 08:28.360
What's up?

08:29.810 --> 08:33.260
I hope you'll keep coaching me 
on this stuff.

08:33.260 --> 08:37.080
I'll do my best to learn...

08:39.950 --> 08:41.430
for you.

08:43.470 --> 08:44.890
Oho?

08:44.890 --> 08:46.540
Wh-What?

08:46.540 --> 08:51.430
You're being awfully 
sweet today. It's adorable.

08:51.710 --> 08:54.130
Do I take that as a compliment?

08:54.560 --> 08:57.430
Usually, I don't think you'd want to.

08:59.270 --> 09:03.270
But you should when it's coming from me.

09:03.830 --> 09:05.270
Okay.

09:08.490 --> 09:10.240
Hey... Umi?

09:10.700 --> 09:11.700
Isn't this...

09:12.160 --> 09:14.030
a couples' seat?

09:15.360 --> 09:18.000
I figured it was okay, 
since we're on a date.

09:18.680 --> 09:20.830
I mean, yeah, but...

09:21.690 --> 09:23.810
Hey, Umi-san?

09:23.810 --> 09:25.280
What is it?

09:25.280 --> 09:28.670
Why'd you cling to my arm 
as soon as we sat down?

09:29.270 --> 09:32.010
When on the couples seat, 
do as the couples do.

09:32.010 --> 09:36.720
Take a look. Pretty much everyone 
in this row is doing the same thing.

09:37.000 --> 09:41.440
Or are you saying you don't want 
to cuddle with me?

09:43.010 --> 09:44.960
I'm not saying that.

09:46.020 --> 09:49.940
You're so shy, Maki. Poke, poke.

09:52.050 --> 09:54.940
Look, the movie's about to start.

09:54.940 --> 09:56.170
Right.

09:57.230 --> 09:58.580
Hey, Maki.

09:58.580 --> 09:59.830
What now?

10:00.100 --> 10:04.390
What if some of our classmates 
see us like this?

10:12.970 --> 10:21.430
KAPPA REAL ESTATE

10:12.970 --> 10:21.430
THE TRAIL YOU LEFT BEHIND

10:12.970 --> 10:21.430
DEAD END SHARK

10:14.210 --> 10:16.100
That was a good nap!

10:16.100 --> 10:18.840
Man, you were out cold within 30 minutes.

10:18.840 --> 10:21.430
I mean, that was godawful!

10:21.430 --> 10:24.990
I came in blind because 
I was excited for today.

10:24.990 --> 10:28.690
Ugh! Of course that's when 
you get a total dud.

10:29.050 --> 10:30.720
The curse of film buffs everywhere.

10:30.720 --> 10:31.860
That's just it!

10:31.860 --> 10:46.790
DEAD END SHARK

10:32.180 --> 10:34.570
Wish we hadn't tried to 
get cute and gone with

10:34.570 --> 10:37.840
the giant cyborg man-eating shark 
versus the all-mighty Gustave

10:37.840 --> 10:41.050
versus the giant deep-sea kraken 
versus the killing spree android

10:41.050 --> 10:44.780
in a titanic battle of superheavyweights!

10:44.780 --> 10:46.790
What's with the all-star lineup?!

10:48.120 --> 10:49.800
Shark!

11:17.860 --> 11:19.510
I'm back.

11:19.510 --> 11:21.700
Whoa!

11:26.110 --> 11:28.160
What'd you think, Maki?

11:28.160 --> 11:31.380
I liked everything, including the dessert.

11:31.800 --> 11:34.060
But I do have one complaint.

11:34.060 --> 11:36.630
Me too, actually.

11:37.210 --> 11:38.720
Wanna say it together?

11:39.490 --> 11:40.600
One, two...

11:40.870 --> 11:42.310
The portions were too small!

11:43.770 --> 11:44.980
I know, right?

11:44.980 --> 11:46.850
Yeah.

11:46.850 --> 11:49.190
I know this is a weird suggestion 
after we just ate,

11:49.570 --> 11:51.590
but how about we go get some burgers?

11:51.590 --> 11:52.900
With fries on the side.

11:52.900 --> 11:56.030
You betcha! Plus onion rings, too!

11:57.470 --> 12:00.320
Hey, Maki. Let's hit up that place.

12:00.810 --> 12:02.060
What place?

12:02.060 --> 12:04.910
Over there, with the red board.

12:04.910 --> 12:06.370
KARAOKE

12:06.750 --> 12:08.330
Karaoke?

12:09.380 --> 12:12.540
What, you don't like singing?

12:12.540 --> 12:15.830
I've actually never been to karaoke.

12:15.830 --> 12:17.820
Today can be your first time, then.

12:17.820 --> 12:18.980
What...

12:18.980 --> 12:20.560
Don't "what" me.

12:21.220 --> 12:24.520
I'm taking you there, 
even if I have to carry you in.

12:26.350 --> 12:28.010
Two hours, with one drink each.

12:28.010 --> 12:30.900
Oh, and give us 
a student discount, please.

12:35.360 --> 12:37.900
How'd you like my angelic voice?

12:37.900 --> 12:40.200
That was great.

12:41.090 --> 12:42.180
Wow!

12:44.650 --> 12:48.290
I haven't sung out loud in a while. 
That felt really good.

12:48.970 --> 12:51.530
Okay, your turn.

12:51.530 --> 12:56.000
Uh, sorry. I don't know 
what I want to sing yet.

12:56.330 --> 13:00.040
No? Want to sing something together, then?

13:00.040 --> 13:00.630
Huh?

13:01.400 --> 13:04.470
That'd make it easier 
for you to sing, right?

13:10.690 --> 13:16.010
Don't Cheat! I'm right by your side

13:16.400 --> 13:21.420
Don't Cheat! It'll just cost you money

13:22.200 --> 13:28.040
Don't Cheat! I'm right by your side

13:28.040 --> 13:32.990
Don't Cheat! 
Because I'll never forgive you

13:39.880 --> 13:43.390
Man, we really went hard singing!

13:46.420 --> 13:49.540
My throat and I can't take any more.

13:49.540 --> 13:50.980
Likewise.

13:52.790 --> 13:55.880
You're actually a pretty 
good singer, Maki.

13:56.310 --> 13:57.860
I have you to thank for it.

13:58.360 --> 14:01.260
It was my first time 
singing in front of anyone,

14:01.260 --> 14:04.610
and you ensured it wouldn't 
be a bitter memory.

14:06.750 --> 14:08.460
Thanks, Umi.

14:08.460 --> 14:10.870
Yeah, you're welcome.

14:13.150 --> 14:15.080
Brr!

14:18.000 --> 14:22.240
You always have a hand warmer 
in your pocket.

14:26.370 --> 14:27.810
Hey, Maki.

14:27.810 --> 14:28.640
Hm?

14:29.610 --> 14:33.790
How do you feel about me?

14:33.790 --> 14:34.960
What do you mean, how?

14:37.270 --> 14:42.280
The kiss on the lips can wait until you 
admit that you like me, okay?

14:44.350 --> 14:48.240
Do you want me to say it now?

14:48.240 --> 14:50.320
I'm not going to force you,

14:50.320 --> 14:53.410
but I do want to hear it 
straight from you.

14:54.670 --> 14:55.560
Is that a problem?

14:56.140 --> 14:58.160
No, it definitely is not.

14:59.000 --> 15:04.930
Then whisper it to me 
so nobody else can hear it.

15:06.840 --> 15:12.340
I don't think I can hold my head high 
and say I'm Umi's boyfriend yet, but...

15:14.230 --> 15:16.140
H-Here I go.

15:16.140 --> 15:18.520
Your breath's tickling me!

15:18.980 --> 15:19.950
Sorry.

15:20.960 --> 15:23.740
Nah, it's okay.

15:25.850 --> 15:26.990
Maehara-san.

15:36.120 --> 15:37.590
Do you know them?

15:38.250 --> 15:41.960
That's my dad and his subordinate at work.

15:41.960 --> 15:43.050
Huh?

15:43.670 --> 15:47.230
They seem awfully close.

15:50.190 --> 15:52.760
Let's get going before they spot us.

15:53.550 --> 15:54.720
Are you sure?

15:55.340 --> 15:58.340
I'd only be a bother if I went to say hi.

15:58.340 --> 16:02.150
And I'm here with you. 
Our date's not over yet—

16:03.400 --> 16:05.050
U-Umi?!

16:05.050 --> 16:06.700
Shh. And don't move.

16:06.700 --> 16:08.530
They're coming this way.

16:21.180 --> 16:22.540
They're gone.

16:23.110 --> 16:24.880
Sorry about that, Umi.

16:25.200 --> 16:29.000
Why apologize? You did nothing wrong.

16:29.000 --> 16:29.620
It's their—

16:29.620 --> 16:33.700
Nah, Dad and Minato-san 
didn't do anything wrong either.

16:33.700 --> 16:36.960
It was just bad timing.

16:40.110 --> 16:44.050
Let's go. Sora-san will start to worry 
if we're out too late.

16:44.590 --> 16:45.520
Yeah.

16:52.880 --> 16:53.940
I'm home.

16:58.910 --> 17:01.170
Oh, welcome back.

17:01.960 --> 17:04.600
Sorry, I did it again.

17:04.600 --> 17:06.500
Again, it doesn't bother me.

17:08.580 --> 17:10.710
Are you tired or something, Mom?

17:10.710 --> 17:11.590
Hm?

17:12.510 --> 17:16.850
I haven't done an end-of-year crunch 
in ages, so it is exhausting.

17:17.450 --> 17:21.160
But if anything, it's the other stuff 
that's taking its toll on me.

17:21.910 --> 17:25.650
By the way, how was 
your date with Umi-chan?

17:26.480 --> 17:27.820
Did it go well?

17:31.200 --> 17:34.900
Yeah, we went to 
the movies and to karaoke.

17:36.020 --> 17:38.400
It was pretty cozy, yeah.

17:38.400 --> 17:42.670
Yeah? Better keep it up 
for Christmas, too.

17:42.670 --> 17:46.070
Oh, but don't try to do what other 
couples do on Christmas Eve.

17:46.070 --> 17:49.590
Say one more word and I'm throwing you 
out onto the balcony, okay?

17:50.710 --> 17:54.300
I'm kidding. I trust you and Umi-chan.

17:54.300 --> 17:55.960
I'm not worried.

17:57.790 --> 17:59.310
Say, Maki.

18:00.370 --> 18:05.870
Do you have any plans next Friday night?

18:05.870 --> 18:11.210
My finals start that day, so I don't.

18:12.130 --> 18:14.660
Well, other than studying for those exams.

18:14.660 --> 18:19.700
Yeah, you do have exams. 
I've been telling him that.

18:19.700 --> 18:21.050
Wait, you mean...

18:21.620 --> 18:27.710
Your dad wants to see you next Friday, 
even though it's a bad time for you.

18:28.730 --> 18:29.660
I see.

18:31.250 --> 18:33.720
During my parents' divorce proceedings,

18:33.720 --> 18:37.440
they negotiated when my dad 
would get to see me.

18:38.120 --> 18:43.060
Until I graduate high school, 
we're to meet about once a month,

18:43.670 --> 18:47.020
get dinner together, 
and give each other life updates.

18:47.610 --> 18:51.210
I didn't come to hate my dad as a 
result of the divorce or anything,

18:51.210 --> 18:53.820
and he usually takes me 
to fancy restaurants,

18:53.820 --> 18:56.770
so I look forward to our meetings.

18:58.470 --> 19:01.580
He usually lets us decide the date, 
but he won't listen this time.

19:02.600 --> 19:06.820
It's fine. He has that right, 
since he gives us financial support.

19:07.310 --> 19:10.900
And that's what allows us 
to live a comfortable life.

19:12.760 --> 19:14.840
Hey, Mom.

19:14.840 --> 19:15.820
What?

19:17.470 --> 19:21.460
I wonder if she knows about Minato-san.

19:22.530 --> 19:25.540
Did their relationship start 
after my dad's divorce,

19:25.540 --> 19:27.970
or was it a long-term thing from before?

19:28.370 --> 19:31.400
If there's any chance it's the latter,

19:31.950 --> 19:35.030
and Mom didn't know about it...

19:32.660 --> 19:35.030
Maki... Maki?

19:35.030 --> 19:35.950
Maki!

19:36.620 --> 19:38.140
Wh-What's the matter?

19:38.690 --> 19:40.870
That's what I want to ask you!

19:41.180 --> 19:44.830
You suddenly went all pale! 
Did the date take it all out of you?

19:45.630 --> 19:50.460
Maybe. I did wake up too early 
out of excitement.

19:50.460 --> 19:55.430
I'll get dinner ready right away. 
You go take a bath first.

19:55.430 --> 19:56.120
Okay.

19:56.470 --> 20:00.300
Oh, and don't keep Umi-chan 
waiting for your text.

20:00.300 --> 20:04.350
You'd better follow up with her 
and thank her for the date.

20:04.620 --> 20:07.920
I know, I know. You're such a nag.

20:10.210 --> 20:13.630
Mom, can I ask you something?

20:13.630 --> 20:14.550
What?

20:15.030 --> 20:18.060
Do you still love Dad?

20:19.710 --> 20:20.890
Why do you ask?

20:20.890 --> 20:24.350
Sorry. It's just, I haven't 
seen Dad in a while.

20:25.530 --> 20:27.630
It got me wondering, 
but should I not have asked?

20:28.390 --> 20:31.000
Nah, it's fine.

20:31.660 --> 20:35.640
Do I still love your dad, huh?

20:36.630 --> 20:38.840
Hm, well...

20:38.840 --> 20:41.620
We went through a lot 
and ended up divorcing,

20:41.620 --> 20:46.560
but deep down, 
I probably do still love him.

20:47.330 --> 20:50.570
Sure, there were times when 
I didn't even want to see his face,

20:50.570 --> 20:54.070
but our photo album 
with pics of all three of us?

20:54.490 --> 20:57.330
I kept it with me. 
I couldn't bring myself to throw it away.

20:58.350 --> 21:00.370
We have a photo album?

21:00.370 --> 21:02.810
Fifteen whole years' worth.

21:03.550 --> 21:07.580
Or actually even more, since we met 
before you were born, of course.

21:09.040 --> 21:11.250
Do you want to check it out later?

21:13.250 --> 21:16.840
MAKI PRESCHOOL ENTRANCE CEREMONY

21:13.250 --> 21:16.840
Wow, I was quite the crybaby at that age.

21:17.200 --> 21:19.190
I don't remember that at all.

21:19.870 --> 21:21.230
You sure were.

21:21.230 --> 21:26.560
When you were little, you'd start wailing 
if anyone other than us picked you up.

21:26.930 --> 21:32.350
FIRST BEACH TRIP

21:27.290 --> 21:31.020
And you'd always hide behind me 
when we took photos.

21:31.020 --> 21:33.010
If we wanted to get 
any good shots of your face,

21:33.010 --> 21:36.320
we had to take them when you were 
too distracted to notice the camera.

21:39.530 --> 21:42.490
HOPEFULLY THE FIRST OF MANY
FUN-FILLED DAYS AT SCHOOL!

21:39.530 --> 21:42.490
Yeah, there's no way I can ask her.

21:40.070 --> 21:42.490
ELEMENTARY SCHOOL
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

21:43.070 --> 21:47.600
Our lives are finally returning to normal.
I don't want to ruin that.

21:48.260 --> 21:51.010
That's the last thing I want right now.

21:51.690 --> 21:55.880
So I won't mention what I saw tonight. 
I'll just forget about it.

21:56.820 --> 22:01.470
I need to do that for Mom... 
and for myself.

21:57.630 --> 22:00.470
MIDDLE SCHOOL
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

21:57.630 --> 22:00.470
CONGRATS ON ENROLLING! YOU
LOOK GREAT IN THAT UNIFORM!

22:01.920 --> 22:04.160
That's what's best for us right now.

